:: Write DiaryB [nobr]

/* 
need to switch to using eventlog in some places for this to work... Or do I? There was also the option of just having "written" tag but I didn't want to do that for some probably good reason... Or was that really what I decided to do? Written seems so much easier to do and I had it in logpars twice even. Main reason for having two things was that it'd mean that what an entry looks like and knows after being written can be very different(one thing being that for written entries I wanted the option to combine multiple ones and have player written text which in addittion to making the diary nicer also allows trimming out more data than otherwise).
Should the eventlog also have day based split? Actually, I think each day knowing the day number could be good in various ways,

*/
You sit down and start writing to your diary.
<<if $log is undefined>>
	<<set $log to $diary>>
<</if>>

<<logcount>>
<<if _unresolved.traumagain gte 10>>
<</if>>
<<if $log.length-1 gt 1>>
It's been <<print 0+$days-$writingday>> days since your last entry it takes you a moment to recall everything that happened.
<</if>>
<br>
<<run console.log("diary write")>>
/*
Day less:
<<for _i to 0; $log[_i][$logpars.written] lt 2 ; _i++>>
<</for>>
*/
<<for _i, _day range $log>>
	<<for _j, _entry range $log[_i]>>
		<<if _entry[$logpars.written] lt 2>>
			<<if _entry[$logpars.stats].traumagain gt 0>>
				!!!
				<<print _entry[$logpars.day]>>
				<<print _entry[$logpars.text]>>
				<br>
				<<run console.log("\_i is:"+_i+" \_j is:"+_j)>>
				/*
				<<run console.log("\_entry is:"+_entry)>>
				<<showlogentry _day _entry>>
				*/
				<<print JSON.stringify($log[_i][_j])>>
				<br><br>
				<<listlogentry _i _j>>
				<br><br>
			<<elseif _entry[$logpars.importance] gt 1>>
				<<listlogentry _i _j>>
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
	<</for>>
<</for>>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<br>
<<showlogentry 0 0>>
<<showlogentry>>
How do you want to write this entry? (carefully written entries about bad events may make you recall them but  
  little effect but also won't help much)
Quickly(0:01)
Normally(0:02)
Carefully(0:05) 
Stop



<<if $rationalisation.deserve isnot undefined>>
	I deserved that.
<<elseif $rationalisation.holy isnot undefined>>
	<<if _resistsuccess isnot 1>>
		My blessings belong to everyone.
	<<else>>
		They didn't deserve my blessing.
	<</if>>
<<elseif $rationalisation.learn isnot undefined>>
	At least I learned something
<<elseif $rationalisation.need isnot undefined>>
	They probably needed that more than I was 
<<elseif $rationalisation.kind isnot undefined>>
	Hopefully they are happier after that. 
<<elseif $rationalisation.polite isnot undefined>>
	<<if _resistsuccess isnot 1>>
		It would have been rude to deny them.
  <<else>>
		It was rude to deny them.
	<</if>>
<<elseif $rationalisation.weak isnot undefined>>
	<<if _resistsuccess isnot 1>>
		I was too weak, it's only right for strong to rule over weak.
	<<else>>
		I proved myself stronger than them.
	<</if>>

<</if>>



Things are better now

